{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The refund is SGD 0.00 on POL-RD-02's own arithmetic, so the rider's claim fails on the money however the threshold question is resolved. Taking the deviation at its highest, recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 17.6 + 0.28 x 28.0) x surge 1.0) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP = SGD 25.64, against a charged_total of SGD 25.26; the refund is charged_total less recomputed_fare floored at zero, which is SGD 0.00, far below the SGD 0.50 de minimis. The fare breakdown's own derived block lands in the same place: recomputed_fare 25.6400, refund_before_rounding 0, refund.payable '0.00', below_de_minimis true, refund_share_of_charged 0.00. The reason is that the optimal route is projected at 28.0 minutes against the 20.2 minutes actually driven, so the optimal-route fare is dearer than the fare charged. Under POL-GEN-03, NO_ACTION on a rider-filed dispute leaves payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 exactly as they stand. The arithmetic rests on EV-FARE-00112, which is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, and on the 17.6 km optimal distance that the rider's own claim_text concedes.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00112", "EV-TRIP-00112"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The facts that produce the zero are not the impaired ones. POL-RD-02's arithmetic runs on charged_total (SGD 25.26), optimal_distance_km (17.6) and optimal_duration_min (28.0), all carried on EV-FARE-00112, which is COMPLETE with weight 1.0 and no issue codes, and the 17.6 km optimal is conceded in the rider's own claim_text. The 0.4 weight on EV-TRIP-00112 and EV-GPS-00112 (CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT) bears only on the excess measurement, which does not decide this outcome. A finding of NO_ACTION therefore does not rest on any artifact below weight 1.0 and does not require the started_at conflict to be resolved.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00112", "EV-GPS-00112"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.charged_total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Measured the way POL-RD-01 prescribes — the gps_trace polyline between the recorded pickup event and the recorded dropoff event — no deviation is established. This trace opens at 18:18:40, thirteen minutes thirty seconds and 2.38 km before the recorded pickup event at started_at 18:32:10, and the admissibility report on EV-TRIP-00112 records that measured from started_at only 20.02 km was driven: an excess of 2.42 km and 13.8%, under the 20% limb of POL-RD-01. Where either establishment test fails no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. The 4.8 km and 27.3% in the derived deviation block is produced only by counting the pre-pickup stretch. The trace is clean on every other measure — gaps [], max_gap_sec 0.0, a 10-second sample interval, 100% coverage — so the defect is one of alignment with the trip record alone. Weight disclosure: EV-GPS-00112 and EV-TRIP-00112 are both IMPAIRED at weight 0.4 with issue CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT, and this claim is made at that discount.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00112", "EV-TRIP-00112"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 0.4
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-06 gives the rider nothing even if a deviation is established. On the highest reading the excess is 4.8 km and 27.3%, which clears the 20% establishment test but neither MATERIAL limb of POL-RD-01 (more than 50%, or more than 8.0 km), so the clause is not engaged at all. And on the two trailing-90-day fields the clause actually names, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 and driver_profile.completed_trips_90d is 296 — far below the 3-flag threshold and far below the 0.05 ratio (1/296 = 0.003) — so no pattern is established and neither the FULL_REFUND uplift nor the driver-conduct referral is available. prior_deviation_flags is a lifetime counter, is not the field POL-RD-06 names, and POL-GEN-01 forbids substituting one for the other. Weight disclosure: the excess figures rest on EV-GPS-00112, IMPAIRED at 0.4, issue CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00112", "EV-GPS-00112"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-RD-01", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 0.4
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's second complaint — that the driver agreed to a Paya Lebar Quarter stop and then skipped it — is not a route-deviation loss and adds nothing to any refund. Her message MSG-00112-001 carries a platform-resolved waypoint_hint at VEN-PAYA-LEBAR-QUARTER and the driver's 'ok can' agrees to it, so on her own account this was a stop she asked for; POL-RD-04 treats a rider-requested detour as exonerated to the extent it adds distance, never as money back. If the stop truly was skipped, then no stop distance was driven and it cannot have inflated this fare. If it was made, then the clause's corroboration limb required the trace to pass within 200 m of the waypoint_hint, and the chat artifact's own admissibility note records that the trace never comes near it — so that limb is not made out, the clause is unavailable, and the case falls back on POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02, where the refund is zero on either branch. Because no monetary outcome turns on this point, this is not the live contradiction of comparable strength that POL-RD-10(7) escalates. Weight disclosure: EV-GPS-00112 is cited at its IMPAIRED weight of 0.4, issue CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00112", "EV-GPS-00112"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "chat_message.waypoint_hint",
      "asserted_weight": 0.4
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-09 adds nothing to the rider's side. The fare breakdown carries erp_gantries [] and erp_lines whose on-optimal-route and off-optimal-route totals are both SGD 0.00, tolls_erp 0.00 and airport_surcharge 0.00 — this trip ENDED at One Raffles Place, so no airport surcharge was chargeable and none was charged. With no ERP, toll or surcharge line charged at all, POL-RD-09(4) has no unmatched line to refund as a standalone pass-through correction, and the rider's only possible recovery on this fare remains the POL-RD-02 figure of zero.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00112"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No LTA advisory covers the PIE or the ECP anywhere in the 18:14-18:52 window on 4 August 2026: EV-ADVIS-00112-01 is MISSING, carries weight 0.0 and the issue MISSING_ARTIFACT. The driver invokes no closure exoneration under POL-RD-03 and needs none, because the refund is zero without any exoneration being run. The absence is cited only to record that neither side can attribute this route to a road closure, and so that no exculpatory clause is said to have been invoked against an artifact missing from the pool.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00112-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Taking the trace on the reading the driver's own account supports — that the app kept showing the trip as not started, so the metered window is short — the driver is owed compensation under POL-RD-04. The fare breakdown bills distance_charged_km of 20.0 while the gps_trace records trace_distance_km of 22.4: an unbilled shortfall of 2.4 km, above the 1.0 km minimum. At SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre that is SGD 1.80, within the SGD 15.00 cap and already a multiple of SGD 0.05. This is the alternative branch of the case: on the other reading, that the trace's opening 2.38 km belongs to an earlier job, the 20.0 km billed matches the 20.02 km driven and this compensation falls away — but on that same reading the rider's excess falls to 13.8% and her claim fails too, so the driver is protected either way. Weight disclosure: EV-GPS-00112 is IMPAIRED at 0.4 with issue CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT, and the trace_distance_km figure is relied on at that discount.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00112", "EV-FARE-00112"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.4
    }
  ]
}
